  body: "# Next stage: semantic map and reviewed journeys\n\nThe first semantic pilot adds explicit relationships
    to individual concept files. All are unreviewed proposals supported by exact captured DWP passages.
    No rule is executable and no staff approval is implied.\n\n[Read the semantic map and evidence register](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/semantic-map.md).
    [Inspect the status, gaps and delivery plan](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/docs/next-stage/README.md).\n\
    \nStart with the capital-disregard candidate and its evidence, duration and assessment-sequence links.
    Compare the projected user questions with the missing evidence and review requirements. CPAG contents
    widen topic discovery only; the handbook text and its legal analysis are not present.\n\nFull DMG
    is a separate acquisition target: 331 PDFs in the metadata census, of which 36 are currently acquired.
    ADM has a separate 182-PDF census. The seminar website and personal-AI/audio connection remain feasibility
    work until actual tool calls and room rehearsal pass.\n\n[Research reference: Capital disregards](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/term/capital-disregards.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Capital disregard: evidence and decision sequence candidate](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/rule-candidate/capital-disregard-sequence.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: What evidence distinguishes guidance from legal interpretation?](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/question/stage2-001.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: What is missing before a candidate rule could be implemented?](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/question/stage2-002.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Which evidence requirements remain operational questions?](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/question/stage2-003.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: How can adviser sources and calculators be compared fairly?](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/question/stage2-004.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: How do application and change journeys need to differ?](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/question/stage2-005.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Can assisted discovery reveal the original and extraction limits?](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/question/stage2-006.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: UK Legislation and Whole-Law OKF](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/resource/okf-uk-legislation.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: CPAG Welfare Benefits Handbook — external reference](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/resource/cpag-welfare-benefits-handbook.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Full Decision makers guide collection](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/resource/full-dmg-collection.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Advice for decision making: staff guide](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/resource/advice-for-decision-making.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Universal Credit: eligibility](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/resource/universal-credit-eligibility.md)."
