- '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/journey/chapter-navigation
  '@type': schema:CreativeWork
  route: journey/chapter-navigation
  title: Follow the guide across chapters
  type: Research navigation
  description: A source-backed route from chapter 77 to connected guidance on additional amounts,
    payments, income and capital. Authored navigation awaiting specialist review.
  body: "# Find the connected guidance\n\nThis project-authored navigation aid follows the signposts in
    chapter 77, paragraph 77003, across PDF pages 3 and 4. Those signposts identify where another topic
    is discussed. They do not establish a claimant's entitlement or show that every condition has been
    captured.\n\n| Research topic | Chapter indicated in paragraph 77003 |\n| --- | --- |\n| Additional
    amounts and special groups | 78 |\n| Payment questions | 79 |\n| Transitional provisions | 80 |\n\
    | Assessed income periods | 83 |\n| Capital and deemed weekly income from capital | 84 |\n| Income
    other than earnings | 85 |\n| Earnings | 86 |\n\nChapter 80 is retained in the source inventory and
    the scope note because it contains transitional provisions. It is not merged into the default seven-chapter
    search corpus. Chapters 81 and 82 are explicitly spare.\n\nParagraph 77003 also points outside this
    two-volume attachment snapshot, including other Decision makers' guide chapters and Advice for decision
    making. External memos and cited legislation require separate acquisition and verification before
    the graph can claim to capture those dependencies.\n\n## Follow an evidence route\n\n1. Open the relevant
    chapter and source page.\n2. Keep definitions, exceptions, dates, examples and footnotes together.\n\
    3. Follow any referenced memo, legislation or other chapter on the official source.\n4. Record which
    dependencies remain unverified before making a domain claim.\n\nThe graph edges from this research
    aid to chapters are authored navigational references. They are not formal legal dependencies or a
    transcription of every cross-reference in the corpus.\n\n\n[Research reference: DMG Vol 13 Ch 77:
    Conditions of entitlement, membership of the household and normal amount payable](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/chapter/77.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: DMG Vol 13 Ch 78: State Pension Credit: additional amounts and special groups
    ](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/chapter/78.md).\n\n[Research
    reference: DMG Vol 13 Ch 79: Payment questions ](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/chapter/79.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: DMG Vol 14 Ch 83: Assessed income periods](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/chapter/83.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: DMG Vol 14 Ch 84: Deemed weekly income from capital](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/chapter/84.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: DMG Vol 14 Ch 85: Income other than earnings ](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/chapter/85.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: DMG Vol 14 Ch 86: Earnings ](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/chapter/86.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Chapter 77 — PDF page 3](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/page/77/0003.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Chapter 77 — PDF page 4](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/page/77/0004.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Transitional, spare and amendment documents](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/guide/source-scope.md)."
