- '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/77/0003
  '@type': schema:DigitalDocument
  id: page/77/0003
  route: page/77/0003
  title: Chapter 77 — PDF page 3
  type: Source PDF page
  description: Introduction 77001 - 77003 Scope of this Chapter 77001 SPC is a SS benefit1 that was
    introduced on 6.10.032. It is made up of 1. a GC, to ensure a minimum level of income for people
    who have reached the qualifying age (see DMG 77330) and 2.
  body: "# DMG Vol 13 Ch 77: Conditions of entitlement, membership of the household and normal amount
    payable — PDF page 3\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68401a731d85c6606009cce4/dmgch77.pdf#page=3).\n\
    \n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not
    establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\nIntroduction 77001 - 77003\n\nScope of this Chapter\n\
    \n77001 SPC is a SS benefit1 that was introduced on 6.10.032. It is made up of\n\n\n1. a GC, to ensure
    a minimum level of income for people who have reached the qualifying age (see DMG\n77330) and\n\n\n\
    2. a SC which, from age 65, provides an additional amount for pensioners who have low or modest\n\
    savings and income (see DMG 77350167).\n\n\nNote 1: See DMG 77031 for guidance on qualifying age.\n\
    \n\nNote 2: From 6.12.183 a person must be at least pensionable age4 (see DMG Chapter 75) to be entitled
    to\na SC.\n\n\n                   1 SPC Act 02, s 1(1); 2 SPC Regs, reg 1(1); 3 Pensions Act 07, s
    13(3); 4 SPC Act 02, s 3(1)\n\n\n77002 This Chapter contains basic guidance on SPC and explains\n\n\
    \n1. the conditions of entitlement for SPC\n\n\n2. how to establish membership of the same household\n\
    \n\n3. how to calculate the normal amount of SPC payable.\n\n\n77003 For guidance on\n\n\n1. the additional
    amounts of GC that may be awarded - see DMG Chapter 78\n\n\n2. the special rules that apply when calculating
    how much SPC to pay\n\n\n        2.1 to members of polygamous marriages - see DMG Chapter 78\n\n\n\
    \        2.2 to prisoners - see DMG Chapter 78\n\n\n        2.3 to members of religious orders - see
    DMG Chapter 78\n\n\n        2.4 when people are in hospital - see DMG Chapter 78\n\n\n        2.5
    when people are subject to the loss of benefit provisions - see ADM Chapter B2\n\n\n        2.6 when
    people are absent from GB - see DMG Chapters 07 and 78\n\n\n3. payment questions - see DMG Chapter
    79\n\n```\n"
