  body: "# DMG Vol 13 Ch 77: Conditions of entitlement, membership of the household and normal amount
    payable — PDF page 5\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68401a731d85c6606009cce4/dmgch77.pdf#page=5).\n\
    \n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not
    establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\nDefinitions 77004 - 77030\n\n\n\nCare home - England
    77005 - 77006\n\n\nCare home - Wales and Scotland 77007 - 77008\n\n\nChild 77009\n\n\nClaimant 77010\n\
    \n\nClose relative 77011 - 77012\n\n\nCouple 77013\n\n\nIndependent hospital 77014\n\n\nPartner 77015\n\
    \n\nPolygamous marriages 77016\n\n\nSpouse 77017\n\n\nYoung person 77018\n\n\nQualifying young person
    77019 - 77028\n\n\nDetermining claims 77029 - 77030\n\n\n\n\n77004 The following paragraphs explain
    the meaning of terms used throughout DMG Volumes 13 and 14\nfor SPC.\n\n\n\nCare home - England\n\n\
    77005 In England, an establishment is a care home 1 if it provides accommodation, together with nursing\n\
    or personal care, for people who\n\n\n1. are or have been ill or\n\n\n2. have or have had a mental
    disorder or\n\n\n3. are disabled or infirm or\n\n```\n"
