  body: "# DMG Vol 13 Ch 78: State Pension Credit: additional amounts and special groups  — PDF page 100\n\
    \n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e10327f5069cdc54868955/dmg-Ch-78.pdf#page=100).\n\
    \n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not
    establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\nPrisoners 78650 - 78679\nIntroduction 78650\n\n\n\
    Meaning of prisoner 78651 - 78660\n\n\nPeriod of detention in custody 78661 - 78662\n\n\nPrisoner
    admitted to hospital 78663\n\n\nClaimant is a Technical Lifer - England and Wales only 78664 -78665\n\
    \n\nGuarantee credit for prisoners 78666\n\n\nGuarantee credit for remand prisoners 78667 - 78671\n\
    \n\nSavings credit for prisoners 78672\n\n\nMembership of the household 78673 - 78679\n\n\n\n\nIntroduction\n\
    \n78650 The amount of SPC payable to a claimant is affected if\n1. the claimant or\n\n\n2. the claimant’s
    partner or\n\n\n3. any additional spouse (in a polygamous marriage case)\n\n\nis, or becomes, a prisoner1.\n\
    \n\n                                        1 SPC Act 02, s 2(3), 2(9) & 3(8); SPC Regs, regs 6(2)(a),
    6(3) & 7(3)\n\n\n\nMeaning of prisoner\n\n78651 A prisoner1 is a person who is detained in custody\n\
    \n\n1. following sentence to a term of imprisonment by a criminal, civil or military court, and includes
    a person\n\n\n      1.1 temporarily removed from prison to hospital, unless DMG 78652 3. applies or\n\
    \n\n      1.2 living outside the prison under a pre-release employment scheme 2 or\n\n```\n"
