    in DMG 78826 3. the only spouse of the claimant’s, the DM should 3.1 revise the award to remove
    all other members of the polygamous marriage from the asses
  body: "# DMG Vol 13 Ch 78: State Pension Credit: additional amounts and special groups  — PDF page 131\n\
    \n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e10327f5069cdc54868955/dmg-Ch-78.pdf#page=131).\n\
    \n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not
    establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\n      2.2 if the spouse in hospital claims SPC in
    their own right, consider their claim as in DMG 78826\n\n\n3. the only spouse of the claimant’s, the
    DM should\n\n\n      3.1 revise the award to remove all other members of the polygamous marriage from
    the\n      assessment and\n\n\n      3.2 if the other members claim SPC, consider their individual
    claims under the normal rules\n\n\n4. the claimant, the DM should\n\n\n      4.1 revise the award
    as in DMG 78826 and\n\n\n      4.2 consider whether a claim should be invited from the remaining members
    and\n\n\n      4.3 if any of the remaining members claims SPC, consider their claims under the normal
    rules.\n\n\n78830 - 78839\n\n```\n"
