  title: Chapter 78 — PDF page 177
  type: Source PDF page
  description: 'Calculation of total weekly income: SPC £60 Total weekly income is £60 Example 5 - Partner
    becomes a prisoner Bernard is aged 68 and lives with his partner Agnes. He is entitled to RP of £127.25
    and occupational pension of £32 a week. He do'
  body: "# DMG Vol 13 Ch 78: State Pension Credit: additional amounts and special groups  — PDF page 177\n\
    \n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e10327f5069cdc54868955/dmg-Ch-78.pdf#page=177).\n\
    \n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not
    establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\nCalculation of total weekly income:\n\n\nSPC   \
    \                   £60\n\n\nTotal weekly income is £60\n\n\n\nExample 5 - Partner becomes a prisoner\n\
    \nBernard is aged 68 and lives with his partner Agnes. He is entitled to RP of £127.25 and occupational\n\
    pension of £32 a week. He does not qualify for any additional amounts and is not entitled to GC but
    gets\nSC of £20.22 a week. So his total weekly income is £179.45. Agnes is detained in custody and
    as a result\nBernard’s RP reduces to £79.60. The DM revises the SPC award to remove Agnes from the
    calculation.\n\n\nCalculation of GC:\n\n\nSMG (claimant with no partner) £105.45\n\n\nAdditional amounts\
    \               Nil\n\n\nAMG                              £105.45\n\n\nLess income (£79.60 + £32)\
    \       £111.60\n\n\nAmount of GC                     Nil\n\n\nCalculation of SC:\n\n\nSCT (claimant
    with no partner)             £79.60\n\n\nQI                                         £111.60\n\n\n\
    QI exceeds SCT by                          £32\n\n\n60% x £32                                  £19.20\n\
    \n\nMSC                                        £\n\n\nAmount A                                   £15.51\n\
    \n\nIncome exceeds AMG by                      £6.25\n\n\nAmount A (£15.51) – Amount B (£2.50) £13.01\n\
    \n\nAmount of SC                               £13.01\n\n```\n"
