  description: Third party deductions for water charges - England and Wales 79660- 79699 Meaning of
    water charges 79660 Methods of charging 79661 Rules for third party deductions 79662 Interests
    of the family 79663-79665 Amount to be deducted and paid dir
  body: "# DMG Vol 13 Ch 79: Payment questions  — PDF page 47\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e1035298c6c9802f7ed9e0/dmg-Chap-79.pdf#page=47).\n\
    \n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not
    establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\nThird party deductions for water charges - England
    and Wales 79660-\n79699\n\n\n\nMeaning of water charges 79660\n\n\nMethods of charging 79661\n\n\n\
    Rules for third party deductions 79662\n\n\nInterests of the family 79663-79665\n\n\nAmount to be
    deducted and paid direct 79666-79669\n\n\nThe original debt 79670\n\n\nUnmetered water 79671-79675\n\
    \n\nMetered water 79676-79682\n\n\nOriginal debt recovered 79683-79684\n\n\nJoint tenants 79685-79686\n\
    \n\nPriority between debts for water charges 79687-79688\n\n\nConsent of claimant required 79689\n\
    \n\nSuperseding the third party deduction decision 79690-79699\n\n\n\n\nMeaning of water charges\n\
    \n79660 For England and Wales water charges means any water or sewerage charges under prescribed\n\
    \nlegislation1. Where these are charged separately or by different water authorities see DMG 79687.\n\
    \n\nNote: The definitions of water charges are different for the purposes of third party deductions
    from\nbenefit (see DMG 79700 for guidance on water charges for Scotland).\n\n\n                  \
    \            1 SS (C&P) Regs, Sch 9, para 1(1), Water Industry Act 1991, Part 5, Chapter 1\n\n```\n"
