  body: "# DMG Vol 14 Ch 85: Income other than earnings  — PDF page 33\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/690b7db588a98da87e292365/dmg-ch-85.pdf#page=33).\n\
    \n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not
    establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\nBenefits taken fully into account 85100 - 85129\n\
    \n\n\nMeaning of social security benefits 85101\n\n\nBereavement allowance 85102\n\n\nCarer’s allowance
    85103\n\n\nESA(Cont) 85104\n\n\nIncapacity benefit 85105 - 85106\n\n\nIndustrial injuries disablement
    benefit 85107 - 85108\n\n\nJSA(Cont)   85109\n\n\nMaternity allowance 85110 - 85111\n\n\nPneumoconiosis,
    byssinosis and miscellaneous diseases benefit scheme 85112 - 85113\n\n\nSevere disablement allowance
    85114\n\n\nWar orphan's pension 85115\n\n\nWidow's pension 85116\n\n\nWorking tax credit 85117 - 85118\n\
    \n\nWorkmen's compensation (supplementation) scheme 85119 - 85129\n\n\n\n\n85100 All SS benefits1,
    apart from a few exceptions2, and WTC are benefits that are taken fully into\naccount.\n\n\n     \
    \                                                               1 SS CB Act 92; 2 SPC Regs, reg 15(1)\n\
    \n\n\nMeaning of social security benefits\n\n85101 SS benefits means1 benefits payable under the enactments
    relating to SS in any part of the United\nKingdom.\n\n\n                                         \
    \                                            1 SPC Act 02, s 17(1)\n\n```\n"
