- '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/85/0039
  '@type': schema:DigitalDocument
  id: page/85/0039
  route: page/85/0039
  title: Chapter 85 — PDF page 39
  type: Source PDF page
  description: Retirement pension income taken fully into account 85130 - 85169 Retirement pension
    85131 - 85132 State Pension 85133 - 85135 Occupational pensions 85136 - 85140 Personal pensions
    85141 - 85142 Retirement annuity contracts 85143 - 85144 Ret
  body: "# DMG Vol 14 Ch 85: Income other than earnings  — PDF page 39\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/690b7db588a98da87e292365/dmg-ch-85.pdf#page=39).\n\
    \n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not
    establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\nRetirement pension income taken fully into account
    85130 - 85169\n\n\n\nRetirement pension 85131 - 85132\n\n\nState Pension 85133 - 85135\n\n\nOccupational
    pensions 85136 - 85140\n\n\nPersonal pensions 85141 - 85142\n\n\nRetirement annuity contracts 85143
    - 85144\n\n\nRetirement annuities purchased on divorce 85145\n\n\nOverseas arrangements 85146 - 85147\n\
    \n\nForeign annuities or insurance policies 85148\n\n\nCivil list pensions 85149 - 85150\n\n\nEquity
    release schemes 85151 - 85152\n\n\nFinancial Assistance Scheme 85153 - 85169\n\n\n\n\n85130 Retirement
    pension income1 includes RP, SP, occupational and personal pensions and certain\nother pension related
    income as explained at DMG 85131 et seq. All retirement pension income should\nbe taken fully into
    account for SPC.\n\n\nNote: Deemed increases in retirement pensions and annuities income (but not
    RP) are explained at DMG\n85052 - 85057.\n\n\n                                                   \
    \                                  1 SPC Act 02, s 16(1)\n\n\n\nRetirement pension\n\n85131 RP should
    be taken fully into account. For SPC purposes this includes either\n\n\n1. contributory (Category
    A or B) RP1 or\n\n\n2. non-contributory (Category C or D) RP2.\n\n\n                             \
    \                                         1 SPC Act 02, s 16(1)(a); 2 s 16(1)(d)\n\n```\n"
  generated:
    by: process:okf-dwp-build/0.1.0
    at: '2026-09-15T14:21:03Z'
