  description: General Rules 86000 - 86027 Introduction 86000 Number of hours worked 86001 Earnings
    of claimant and partner 86002 Polygamous marriages 86003 Rounding of fractions 86004 Effect of
    earnings 86005 - 86018 Final payments of income 86019 - 8602
  body: "# DMG Vol 14 Ch 86: Earnings  — PDF page 2\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/698462dd468d351e1406b4a7/dmgch86.pdf#page=2).\n\
    \n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not
    establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\nGeneral Rules 86000 - 86027\nIntroduction 86000\n\
    \n\nNumber of hours worked 86001\n\n\nEarnings of claimant and partner 86002\n\n\nPolygamous marriages
    86003\n\n\nRounding of fractions 86004\n\n\nEffect of earnings 86005 - 86018\n\n\nFinal payments of
    income 86019 - 86023\n\n\nArrears of earnings 86024 - 86025\n\n\nPart week payments 86026 - 86027\n\
    \n\n\n\nIntroduction\n\n86000 This chapter deals with the calculation and treatment of earnings in
    claims for SPC. For SPC\n\nearnings1 include\n\n\n1. earnings of employed earners2\n\n\n2. earnings
    from self-employment3.\n\n\n1 SPC Act 02, s 17(1), SS CB Act 92, Pt 1 to 5; 2 SPC Regs, reg 17A; 3
    Reg 17B, SS Ben (C of E) Regs, reg 11\n\n\n\n\nNumber of hours worked\n\n86001 For the purposes of
    SPC a claimant may work for any number of hours each week without\nentitlement being affected. The
    earnings from such employment will however affect the amount of SPC\nto which the claimant will be
    entitled.\n\n```\n"
