  description: Introduction 86028 - 86030 86028 This part deals with the calculation and treatment
    of payments made to SPC claimants who are employed earners. These will usually be earnings paid
    by an employer, but may be other types of payment. 86029 How
  body: "# DMG Vol 14 Ch 86: Earnings  — PDF page 13\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/698462dd468d351e1406b4a7/dmgch86.pdf#page=13).\n\
    \n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not
    establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\nIntroduction 86028 - 86030\n\n\n\n86028 This part
    deals with the calculation and treatment of payments made to SPC claimants who are\nemployed earners.
    These will usually be earnings paid by an employer, but may be other types of\npayment.\n\n\n86029
    How payments made to employees affect a claim to SPC will depend on\n\n\n1. whether the work is continuing
    or\n\n\n2. whether the work has ended.\n\n\n86030 Earnings from employment as an employed earner which
    is ongoing whilst the claimant is in\nreceipt of SPC are taken into account, less any appropriate
    earnings disregard, in the same way as other\nincome.\n\n```\n"
