  description: Carers 86116 £20 of earnings should be disregarded where the 1. claimant or 2.
    partner or 3. both the claimant and partner are carers1. 1 SPC Regs, Sch VI, para 3(1) 86117 The
    claimant or partner is a carer for the purposes of the £20 disre
  body: "# DMG Vol 14 Ch 86: Earnings  — PDF page 36\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/698462dd468d351e1406b4a7/dmgch86.pdf#page=36).\n\
    \n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not
    establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\nCarers\n\n86116 £20 of earnings should be disregarded
    where the\n\n\n1. claimant or\n\n\n2. partner or\n\n\n3. both the claimant and partner\n\n\nare carers1.\n\
    \n\n                                                                                1 SPC Regs, Sch
    VI, para 3(1)\n\n\n86117 The claimant or partner is a carer for the purposes of the £20 disregard
    if their SPC includes an\n\nadditional amount in accordance with DMG 781001.\n\n\n               \
    \                                                                 1 SPC Regs, Sch VI, para 3(2)\n\n\
    \n\nDisabled people\n\n86118 [See Memo DMG 06/25] A disregard of £20 per week applies where a claimant
    or their partner\n\n\n1. is in receipt of\n\n\n       1.1 long term IB1\n\n\n       1.2 SDA2\n\n\n\
    \       1.3 “AA”3\n\n\n       1.4 DLA4\n\n\n       1.5 mobility supplement5\n\n\n       1.6 the disability
    or severe disability elements of WTC6\n\n\n       1.7 ESA7\n\n\n       1.8 PIP8\n\n\n       1.9 AFIP9
    or\n\n\n2. is certified as severely sight impaired or blind by a consultant ophthalmologist 10 or\n\
    \n```\n"
