- '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/persona/policy-law-reviewer
  route: persona/policy-law-reviewer
  title: Policy and legislation reviewer
  type: Persona
  description: Projected reviewer who distinguishes operational guidance, legal sources and
    project-authored interpretation.
  status: draft
  tags:
  - unofficial
  - project-authored
  - persona
  - projected-persona
  - staff-derived-need
  - ST01
  generated:
    by: process:codex-research-authoring
    at: '2026-09-15T16:53:17Z'
  body: "# Policy and legislation reviewer\n\nThis projected persona derives from a de-identified staff
    need to distinguish policy and legislation and investigate ambiguity. It has not been validated through
    user research.\n\nGoal: inspect the evidence supporting an interpretation, its temporal and jurisdictional
    scope, and the gaps requiring review. A reported operational preference for consulting guidance first
    is not a statement that guidance overrides legislation.\n\nSuccess requires exact source locators,
    clear source types and visible unresolved dependencies. No policy or legal approval is implied by
    this record.\n\n\n[Research reference: Trace guidance and legal references](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/story/policy-law-trace.md)."
  id: persona/policy-law-reviewer
  '@type': schema:Role
  authority: model-assisted research navigation; unreviewed
  dcterms:references:
  - '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/story/policy-law-trace
- '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/persona/rules-architect
  route: persona/rules-architect
  title: Rules architect
  type: Persona
  description: Projected architect who needs a reviewable chain from evidence to a proposed rule and
    independent synthetic tests.
  status: draft
  tags:
  - unofficial
  - project-authored
  - persona
  - projected-persona
  - staff-derived-need
  - ST02
  - MP01
  generated:
    by: process:codex-research-authoring
    at: '2026-09-15T16:53:17Z'
  body: "# Rules architect\n\nThis projected persona reflects the staff's interest in a guidance-based
    rules engine. The evidence → proposition → rule → executable rule method is a quoted model proposal
    for evaluation, not an agreed architecture.\n\nGoal: identify which stages exist, inspect traceability
    and determine what prevents a candidate from becoming executable. Conditions, exceptions, temporal
    scope, source changes and review decisions must be visible.\n\nThis exemplar does not establish a
    production technology choice, a complete engine or an agreed delivery estimate.\n\n\n[Research reference:
    Review an evidence-backed rule candidate](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/story/rule-candidate-review.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Audit a source transformation](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/story/evidence-audit.md)."
  id: persona/rules-architect
  '@type': schema:Role
  authority: model-assisted research navigation; unreviewed
  dcterms:references:
  - '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/story/rule-candidate-review
  - '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/story/evidence-audit
