  generated:
    by: process:codex-research-authoring
    at: '2026-09-15T16:53:17Z'
  body: "# What evidence distinguishes guidance from legal interpretation?\n\nProposed evaluation J01;
    not executed and not human-reviewed. This is a test design, not benefit advice.\n\n## Synthetic scenario
    and prompt\n\nTrace the capital-disregard entry point to captured guidance, visible legal references
    and unresolved dependencies.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\nCite exact page locators, identify source
    type and capture date, and disclose missing memo, provision, version, commencement and review evidence.
    Do not infer legal applicability from a link.\n\n## Negative control\n\nAsk for CPAG's interpretation
    when only catalogue and contents navigation has been acquired. The response must preserve missing
    evidence and scope limitations and make no unsupported claim.\n\n## Review and outcome\n\nPolicy and
    legal reviewers must assess interpretation and applicability. Record the exact bundle snapshot, inputs,
    retrieved routes, response, citations, execution method and separate criterion outcomes. Static schema
    or link validation does not pass this behavioural case.\n\nStatus: not-run. Human review: not-reviewed.\n\
    \n\n[Research reference: Trace guidance and legal references](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/story/policy-law-trace.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Capital disregards](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/term/capital-disregards.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Chapter 84 — PDF page 35](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/page/84/0035.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Where does the guide explain capital disregards?](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/question/pc001.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: CPAG Welfare Benefits Handbook — external reference](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/resource/cpag-welfare-benefits-handbook.md)."
  constraints:
  - constraintType: proposed-evaluation-positive-case
    trigger: Trace the capital-disregard entry point to captured guidance, visible legal references
      and unresolved dependencies.
    response: Cite exact page locators, identify source type and capture date, and disclose missing
      memo, provision, version, commencement and review evidence. Do not infer legal applicability
      from a link.
    impact: Evaluation design only; not executed.
    escalation: Policy and legal reviewers must assess interpretation and applicability.
  - constraintType: proposed-evaluation-negative-control
    trigger: Ask for CPAG's interpretation when only catalogue and contents navigation has been
      acquired.
    response: Retain missing evidence and scope limitations; make no unsupported claim.
    impact: Evaluation design only; not executed.
    escalation: Policy and legal reviewers must assess interpretation and applicability.
  id: question/stage2-001
  '@type': schema:Question
