    at: '2026-09-15T16:53:17Z'
  body: "# Which evidence requirements remain operational questions?\n\nProposed evaluation J03; not executed
    and not human-reviewed. This is a test design, not benefit advice.\n\n## Synthetic scenario and prompt\n\
    \nFor an invented household change, separate policy topics from operational evidence requirements
    that need an authorised owner.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\nLabel requirements as source-backed, stakeholder-derived
    or unresolved; identify review ownership and ask for no real personal data.\n\n## Negative control\n\
    \nAssert that one policy passage necessarily requires a particular identity document or a fraud score
    without separate supporting evidence. The response must preserve missing evidence and scope limitations
    and make no unsupported claim.\n\n## Review and outcome\n\nOperational evidence, fraud and error,
    privacy and policy specialists must review within their remit. Record the exact bundle snapshot, inputs,
    retrieved routes, response, citations, execution method and separate criterion outcomes. Static schema
    or link validation does not pass this behavioural case.\n\nStatus: not-run. Human review: not-reviewed.\n\
    \n\n[Research reference: Separate policy and operational evidence needs](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/story/evidence-requirements.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Membership of the household](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/term/household.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: DMG Vol 13 Ch 77: Conditions of entitlement, membership of the household and
    normal amount payable](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/chapter/77.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Spot historical and missing context](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/story/context-review.md)."
  constraints:
  - constraintType: proposed-evaluation-positive-case
    trigger: For an invented household change, separate policy topics from operational evidence
      requirements that need an authorised owner.
    response: Label requirements as source-backed, stakeholder-derived or unresolved; identify
      review ownership and ask for no real personal data.
    impact: Evaluation design only; not executed.
    escalation: Operational evidence, fraud and error, privacy and policy specialists must review
      within their remit.
  - constraintType: proposed-evaluation-negative-control
    trigger: Assert that one policy passage necessarily requires a particular identity document or a
      fraud score without separate supporting evidence.
    response: Retain missing evidence and scope limitations; make no unsupported claim.
    impact: Evaluation design only; not executed.
    escalation: Operational evidence, fraud and error, privacy and policy specialists must review
      within their remit.
