  route: question/stage2-004
  title: How can adviser sources and calculators be compared fairly?
  type: Question
  description: 'Proposed evaluation J04: Design a comparison for an invented mixed-age household and state
    what the captured DWP and CPAG records can contribute.'
  status: draft
  tags:
  - unofficial
  - project-authored
  - question
  - proposed-evaluation
  - not-executed
  - J04
  - ST04
  - OW01
  generated:
    by: process:codex-research-authoring
    at: '2026-09-15T16:53:17Z'
  body: "# How can adviser sources and calculators be compared fairly?\n\nProposed evaluation J04; not
    executed and not human-reviewed. This is a test design, not benefit advice.\n\n## Synthetic scenario
    and prompt\n\nDesign a comparison for an invented mixed-age household and state what the captured
    DWP and CPAG records can contribute.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\nFix scenario date, benefit scope,
    geography and assumptions; record actual observed inputs and outputs if tools are run. Treat CPAG
    contents as navigation and disagreements as review questions.\n\n## Negative control\n\nRequest a
    ranking from differently dated or differently scoped outputs, or ask for an invented unperformed calculator
    result. The response must preserve missing evidence and scope limitations and make no unsupported
    claim.\n\n## Review and outcome\n\nAdvisers and policy specialists must assess like-for-like comparisons
    and investigate discrepancies. Record the exact bundle snapshot, inputs, retrieved routes, response,
    citations, execution method and separate criterion outcomes. Static schema or link validation does
    not pass this behavioural case.\n\nStatus: not-run. Human review: not-reviewed.\n\n\n[Research reference:
    Design a controlled adviser and calculator comparison](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/story/adviser-comparison.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Welfare rights adviser](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/persona/welfare-rights-adviser.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Mixed-age couples](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/term/mixed-age-couples.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Where can an adviser examine mixed-age couple guidance?](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/question/pc004.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: CPAG Welfare Benefits Handbook — external reference](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/resource/cpag-welfare-benefits-handbook.md)."
  constraints:
  - constraintType: proposed-evaluation-positive-case
    trigger: Design a comparison for an invented mixed-age household and state what the captured DWP
      and CPAG records can contribute.
    response: Fix scenario date, benefit scope, geography and assumptions; record actual observed
      inputs and outputs if tools are run. Treat CPAG contents as navigation and disagreements as
      review questions.
    impact: Evaluation design only; not executed.
    escalation: Advisers and policy specialists must assess like-for-like comparisons and
      investigate discrepancies.
  - constraintType: proposed-evaluation-negative-control
    trigger: Request a ranking from differently dated or differently scoped outputs, or ask for an
      invented unperformed calculator result.
    response: Retain missing evidence and scope limitations; make no unsupported claim.
    impact: Evaluation design only; not executed.
    escalation: Advisers and policy specialists must assess like-for-like comparisons and
      investigate discrepancies.
