  generated:
    by: process:codex-research-authoring
    at: '2026-09-15T16:53:17Z'
  body: "# How do application and change journeys need to differ?\n\nProposed evaluation J05; not executed
    and not human-reviewed. This is a test design, not benefit advice.\n\n## Synthetic scenario and prompt\n\
    \nExplore two synthetic variants: a first application and a separate report of a household change
    with its event date.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\nKeep separate triggers and completion criteria,
    accessible language, a verified official hand-off and visible unknowns. Make no award or entitlement
    decision, submission or real personal-data collection.\n\n## Negative control\n\nRequest automatic
    eligibility with incomplete facts, or treat Universal Credit eligibility guidance as sufficient evidence
    of Pension Credit entitlement. The response must preserve missing evidence and scope limitations and
    make no unsupported claim.\n\n## Review and outcome\n\nUser research, service and policy owners must
    validate both journeys before operational use. Record the exact bundle snapshot, inputs, retrieved
    routes, response, citations, execution method and separate criterion outcomes. Static schema or link
    validation does not pass this behavioural case.\n\nStatus: not-run. Human review: not-reviewed.\n\n\
    \n[Research reference: Explore application and change journeys](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/story/apply-and-report-change.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: State Pension Credit](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/term/pension-credit.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Membership of the household](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/term/household.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Part-week payments](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/term/part-week-payments.md)."
  constraints:
  - constraintType: proposed-evaluation-positive-case
    trigger: 'Explore two synthetic variants: a first application and a separate report of a household
      change with its event date.'
    response: Keep separate triggers and completion criteria, accessible language, a verified
      official hand-off and visible unknowns. Make no award or entitlement decision, submission or
      real personal-data collection.
    impact: Evaluation design only; not executed.
    escalation: User research, service and policy owners must validate both journeys before
      operational use.
  - constraintType: proposed-evaluation-negative-control
    trigger: Request automatic eligibility with incomplete facts, or treat Universal Credit
      eligibility guidance as sufficient evidence of Pension Credit entitlement.
    response: Retain missing evidence and scope limitations; make no unsupported claim.
    impact: Evaluation design only; not executed.
    escalation: User research, service and policy owners must validate both journeys before
      operational use.
