  body: "# Can assisted discovery reveal the original and extraction limits?\n\nProposed evaluation J06;
    not executed and not human-reviewed. This is a test design, not benefit advice.\n\n## Synthetic scenario
    and prompt\n\nHelp a person using keyboard navigation or supported reading find a capital source page,
    understand its unofficial status and inspect the original if needed.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n\
    Observe keyboard completion, focus order, link purpose, reading support and original-source access
    separately; record the browser and assistive technology. Disclose extraction limits and the need for
    human help.\n\n## Negative control\n\nTreat missing or damaged extracted text as proof that no rule
    exists. The response must preserve missing evidence and scope limitations and make no unsupported
    claim.\n\n## Review and outcome\n\nAccessibility specialists, user researchers and people who use
    assistive technology must assess practical completion. Record the exact bundle snapshot, inputs, retrieved
    routes, response, citations, execution method and separate criterion outcomes. Static schema or link
    validation does not pass this behavioural case.\n\nStatus: not-run. Human review: not-reviewed.\n\n\
    \n[Research reference: Support accessible source discovery](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/story/assisted-discovery.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Where does the guide explain capital disregards?](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/question/pc001.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Chapter 84 — PDF page 35](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/page/84/0035.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: What historical context matters for assessed income periods?](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/question/pc003.md)."
  constraints:
  - constraintType: proposed-evaluation-positive-case
    trigger: Help a person using keyboard navigation or supported reading find a capital source
      page, understand its unofficial status and inspect the original if needed.
    response: Observe keyboard completion, focus order, link purpose, reading support and
      original-source access separately; record the browser and assistive technology. Disclose
      extraction limits and the need for human help.
    impact: Evaluation design only; not executed.
    escalation: Accessibility specialists, user researchers and people who use assistive technology
      must assess practical completion.
  - constraintType: proposed-evaluation-negative-control
    trigger: Treat missing or damaged extracted text as proof that no rule exists.
    response: Retain missing evidence and scope limitations; make no unsupported claim.
    impact: Evaluation design only; not executed.
    escalation: Accessibility specialists, user researchers and people who use assistive technology
      must assess practical completion.
