  body: "# CPAG Welfare Benefits Handbook\n\n**External reference — metadata and links only. Handbook
    text is not included.**\n\nPublisher: Child Poverty Action Group (CPAG). CPAG's [online handbook catalogue](https://cpag.org.uk/welfare-rights/online-handbooks)
    lists the Welfare Benefits Handbook for subscribers. [Open the handbook on AskCPAG](https://askcpag.org.uk/publications/-268900/welfare-benefits-handbook-2026-27).\n\
    \nThe publisher describes the 2026/27 edition as released in **April 2026**; CPAG announced online
    availability on **6 April 2026**. These are source-publication metadata, not the project capture date
    or a legal effective date. The linked URL was first observed by this project on **15 September 2026**.
    Month precision is retained for publication; a day is not inferred. Subscriber contents have not been
    acquired. [Publisher release statement](https://cpag.org.uk/shop/subscription/print-subscription);
    [online availability announcement](https://cpag.org.uk/welfare-rights/whats-new). CPAG's public [housing-costs
    topic index](https://cpag.org.uk/welfare-rights/key-topics/housing-costs) links a Pension Credit chapter,
    making this a relevant adviser reference.\n\n## Access and reuse\n\nCPAG's [terms and conditions](https://cpag.org.uk/terms-and-conditions),
    subscription clause 9.3, require prior written consent to incorporate subscription content into AI
    tools or automated processes. Website clauses 6.2, 11.2 and 12 address reproduction, permission requests
    and automated reuse. See the [access review](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/docs/cpag-handbook.md).\n\
    \nThis record provides a route for an authorised reader to consult CPAG. No handbook passages, legal
    propositions, rules or calculations have been extracted. Its topic relationship is project-authored
    navigation and does not establish agreement between CPAG and DWP. Original catalogue commentary here
    is MIT-licensed; CPAG's book is not covered by this project's MIT licence or the GOV.UK Open Government
    Licence.\n\n\n[Research reference: State Pension Credit](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/term/pension-credit.md)."
  modified: '2026-09-15T17:15:00Z'
