- '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/rule-candidate/capital-disregard-sequence
  route: rule-candidate/capital-disregard-sequence
  title: 'Capital disregard: evidence and decision sequence candidate'
  type: RuleCandidate
  status: draft
  authority: project-authored review candidate; not executable
  generated:
    by: process:codex-semantic-stage-two
    at: '2026-09-15T16:57:46Z'
  observedAt: '2026-09-15T16:57:46Z'
  description: A review packet tracing DMG 84351–84356 to concepts, evidence needs, duration and a
    proposed decision sequence. No entitlement result is produced.
  tags:
  - capital disregards
  - rule candidate
  - review required
  body: "# Capital disregard: evidence and decision sequence candidate\n\n**Review state: unreviewed.
    Executable: no.**\n\n## Proposition to review\n\nThe captured guidance separates whether an item can
    be disregarded, the evidence for it and its duration. DMG 84355 places the disregard decision before
    valuation and before deemed weekly income is calculated. These are source-bound propositions, not
    findings about a claimant or an assurance of current law.\n\n## Proposed review sequence\n\n1. Identify
    the asset, relevant ownership, benefit and decision date.\n2. Identify the applicable disregard category
    and supporting evidence.\n3. Review the legal basis, amendments, commencement, territorial scope,
    DMG Memo 11/20 and any applicable decisions.\n4. Have a domain reviewer determine whether the disregard
    and period are supported; record missing or disputed evidence.\n5. Only then assess how valuation
    and deemed income should be represented for the agreed rule family.\n\nDo not infer that an unanswered
    field proves ineligibility. Do not apply the Pension Credit sequence to Universal Credit through name
    similarity.\n\n## Still required before an executable rule\n\nNamed policy and legal reviewers; the
    missing original stakeholder plan; acquired and checked provisions and memo; exceptions; effective
    dates; evidence/fraud/error requirements; review and appeal paths; synthetic positive, negative and
    boundary cases; independently accepted expected outcomes. A model-generated expected answer is not
    a gold standard.\n\nThe official instrument links identify candidate sources cited in the guidance.
    Their provisions and amendment effects have not been consolidated in this bundle.\n\n\n[Research reference:
    Capital disregards](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/term/capital-disregards.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Evidence for a capital disregard](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/term/capital-disregard-evidence.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Period of a capital disregard](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/term/capital-disregard-period.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Valuation of capital](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/term/capital-valuation.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Deemed weekly income from capital](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/term/deemed-weekly-income.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Chapter 84 — PDF page 35](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/page/84/0035.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Chapter 84 — PDF page 36](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/page/84/0036.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: State Pension Credit Act 2002](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/resource/state-pension-credit-act-2002.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: The State Pension Credit Regulations 2002](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/resource/state-pension-credit-regulations-2002.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: What is missing before a candidate rule could be implemented?](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/question/stage2-002.md)."
  id: rule-candidate/capital-disregard-sequence
  '@type': schema:CreativeWork
  dcterms:references:
  - '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/term/capital-disregards
  - '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/term/capital-disregard-evidence
