  generated:
    by: process:codex-research-authoring
    at: '2026-09-15T16:53:17Z'
  body: "# Design a controlled adviser and calculator comparison\n\nProposed journey J04, addressing staff
    need ST04. Define a controlled comparison with an invented mixed-age household, a fixed scenario date,
    benefit scope, geography and assumptions.\n\nAcceptance: record actual tool inputs, observed outputs,
    dates or versions and limitations if a calculator is later run. Distinguish DWP source evidence from
    CPAG catalogue and contents navigation. Treat disagreements as questions for review.\n\nNo calculator
    run or substantive CPAG analysis is claimed by this story. Adviser and policy review must establish
    whether comparisons are useful and like-for-like.\n\n\n[Research reference: Welfare rights adviser](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/persona/welfare-rights-adviser.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Mixed-age couples](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/term/mixed-age-couples.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: CPAG Welfare Benefits Handbook — external reference](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/resource/cpag-welfare-benefits-handbook.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: How can adviser sources and calculators be compared fairly?](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/question/stage2-004.md)."
  id: story/adviser-comparison
  '@type': schema:CreativeWork
  authority: model-assisted research navigation; unreviewed
