    at: '2026-09-15T16:53:17Z'
  body: "# Support accessible source discovery\n\nProposed journey J06, extending the owner's customer-journey
    request. Help a person find a source page, understand the unofficial record and recognise damaged
    or missing extracted text.\n\nAcceptance: observe keyboard completion, focus order, link purpose,
    reading support and access to the original. Record the actual browser and assistive technology used.
    A tool-generated page snapshot alone does not demonstrate accessibility.\n\nWhere extraction is unclear,
    identify the original-source route and need for human support. Accessibility specialists and people
    who use assistive technology must validate practical task completion.\n\n\n[Research reference: Assisted
    support practitioner](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/persona/assisted-support.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Where does the guide explain capital disregards?](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/question/pc001.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: What historical context matters for assessed income periods?](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/question/pc003.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Can assisted discovery reveal the original and extraction limits?](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/question/stage2-006.md)."
  id: story/assisted-discovery
