    at: '2026-09-15T16:53:17Z'
  body: "# Trace guidance and legal references\n\nProposed journey J01, addressing staff need ST01 and
    owner request OW01. Start with the capital-disregard entry point and distinguish captured DWP guidance
    from legal references and project-authored interpretation.\n\nAcceptance: retain original page links,
    capture dates, source types and unresolved memo or legislation dependencies. A legal link must disclose
    whether it identifies a work, provision or verified dated version.\n\nCPAG's captured navigation supplies
    no substantive interpretation. A policy specialist and legal reviewer must assess interpretation and
    applicability before any review status is advanced.\n\n\n[Research reference: Policy and legislation
    reviewer](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/persona/policy-law-reviewer.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Capital disregards](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/term/capital-disregards.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: Chapter 84 — PDF page 35](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/page/84/0035.md).\n\
    \n[Research reference: What evidence distinguishes guidance from legal interpretation?](https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/bundle/records/question/stage2-001.md)."
  id: story/policy-law-trace
