      https://github.com/chris-page-gov/okf-dwp/blob/main/knowledge/concepts/deprivation-of-capital.yamlld
    source_artifact: knowledge/concepts/deprivation-of-capital.yamlld
    source_sha256: 9e2b84c10febfc6d2aecea7ce06e1edb3ebb83ee0f9bea63e1cfbd5afc031966
    source_field: term/deprivation-of-capital.semantic_relations[0]
    source_value: '{"evidence":[{"locator":"DMG 84781","page":"page/84/0111","quote":"84781 People should
      be treated as having capital they do not have if they deprive themselves of their\n\ncapital for
      the purpose of getting SPC or more SPC 1. People are not treated as having the amount by\n\nwhich
      notional capital is reduced under the diminishing notional capital rule 2. People have not deprived\nthemselves
      of capital if they disposed of it\n\n\n1. to reduce or pay a debt owed by themselves3 or\n\n\n2.
      to buy goods or services and it was reasonable in their case to buy such goods or services 4."}],"predicate":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related","rationale":"The
      source relates deprivation to treatment of notional capital and explicitly includes exceptions;
      the edge does not decide intention or deprivation.","target":"term/notional-capital"}'
