    source_value: '{"evidence":[{"locator":"DMG 84355","page":"page/84/0036","quote":"84355 The DM decides
      if capital can be disregarded. This is done\n\n\n1. before the capital is valued as the DM does
      not have to know the value of the capital to decide if it can\nbe disregarded and\n\n\n2. before
      working out the amount of deemed weekly income from capital.\n\n\nThe DM also decides how long the
      capital is disregarded and, for certain disregards, whether it is\nreasonable to disregard the capital
      for a longer period."}],"predicate":"https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/ns#precedesAssessmentOf","rationale":"This
